[B]About[/B]

This is an unofficial CyanogenMod 10.1 port for the [B]Huawei Y220-U05[/B] (MediaTek MT6572), based on Android 4.2.2 Jelly Bean. The phone ships with Android 2.3.6, but the MT6572 is a Jelly Bean-era chip: other phones built on it shipped with 4.2. So instead of forcing the Gingerbread blobs into Jelly Bean, this ROM uses the Android 4.2.2 MediaTek userspace of another MT6572 Huawei, the [B]Ascend Y330-U01[/B] (same SoC, same Mali-400 r3p2 driver, kernel modules with the same version as the Y220's). The modem, the Wi-Fi/Bluetooth firmware and the camera tuning stay the Y220's own.

The CyanogenMod 10.1 platform is untouched: no framework or system patches. Everything Y220-specific lives in the device tree. The kernel is the same Linux 3.4.5 built from source as in my CM7 port.

[COLOR="Red"][B]This ROM is only for Huawei Y220-U05. It is not compatible with Huawei Y210 or Y330.[/B][/COLOR]

[SIZE="4"][B]Current status — Beta 1[/B][/SIZE]

Build: [B]cm-10.1-20261024-UNOFFICIAL-y220-beta1.zip[/B] (userdebug)
Kernel: Linux 3.4.5 #98
MD5: [B]ce0c5c2bd2bcbcdbd71b5c090b979c8d[/B]

Everything listed below was checked on real hardware. Please report anything that does not work.

[SIZE="4"][B]What's working[/B][/SIZE]

[LIST]
[*][B]Phone:[/B] voice calls (outgoing, incoming, hold, also with mobile data on), USSD codes, SIM, operator registration, signal bars, SMS (send and receive), mobile data (EDGE; it also registers on HSPA)
[*][B]Wi-Fi:[/B] scan, connect (WPA/WPA2), DHCP, internet
[*][B]Bluetooth:[/B] pairing, music to headphones (A2DP), calls through a Bluetooth headset, factory address
[*][B]Audio:[/B] speaker, microphone and recording
[*][B]Camera:[/B] preview, photos and video recording (640x480; 0.3 MP rear camera, the phone has no front camera and no flash)
[*][B]Display / GPU:[/B] Mali-400 MP, OpenGL ES 2.0, 320x480
[*][B]Input:[/B] touchscreen, capacitive back/home/menu keys, volume and power keys
[*][B]Sensors:[/B] accelerometer (rotation), vibration
[*][B]Storage:[/B] UBIFS system/data/cache, microSD, USB (adb, mass storage)
[*][B]Tethering:[/B] USB tethering and Wi-Fi hotspot
[*][B]Charging with the phone off[/B], with the original Huawei charging animation
[*][B]zram swap[/B] (about 190 MB, same as stock), deep sleep
[/LIST]

[SIZE="4"][B]Known issues[/B][/SIZE]

[LIST]
[*][B]Video recording[/B] is 640x480 at up to 15 fps (software encoder), fewer in low light.
[*][B]Video playback[/B] uses the software decoders. The MediaTek hardware decoders would need a CyanogenMod framework patch.
[*][B]MMS:[/B] not tested yet.
[*][B]FM radio:[/B] not included.
[*]Jelly Bean on 256 MB of RAM is tighter than CM7. zram helps, but heavy apps will be closed in the background.
[*]The phone has no GPS, compass, proximity or light sensor, same as stock.
[/LIST]

