[SIZE="4"][B]Installation[/B][/SIZE]

[COLOR="Red"][B]Back up NVRAM (IMEI, Wi-Fi and Bluetooth addresses) and your complete current system before flashing. Do not use Format All in SP Flash Tool, and do not use SP Flash Tool v6.[/B][/COLOR]

[LIST=1]
[*]Install [URL="https://xdaforums.com/t/recovery-unofficial-twrp-3-1-1-0-1-for-huawei-y220-u05.4805984/"]TWRP 3.1.1-0.1 for Huawei Y220-U05[/URL].
[*]Copy the ROM ZIP to the external microSD (it needs about 140 MB free; if the card is full, push it with adb to /data after the wipe in step 4 and delete it after installing).
[*]Boot into TWRP and make a complete backup to the external microSD, including the NVRAM partitions (nvram, protect_f, protect_s).
[*]Wipe cache and Dalvik cache, and wipe data [B]keeping /data/nvram[/B] (see below).
[*]Install the ROM ZIP.
[*]Reboot. The first boot takes a few minutes.
[/LIST]

After a clean install the phone shows up on USB as mass storage with adb on (userdebug build). The first time you connect it, accept the computer's key on the phone ("Allow USB debugging?").

[B]Wiping data without losing NVRAM:[/B] /data/nvram holds the IMEI and the Wi-Fi/Bluetooth calibration files. From TWRP, with adb:
[CODE]adb shell
mount /data
cd /data && for e in * .[!.]*; do [ "$e" = nvram ] || rm -rf "$e"; done
rm -rf /cache/*[/CODE]

[B]Coming from CM7 or stock:[/B] a data wipe is required (Gingerbread to Jelly Bean).

[B]UBIFS warning:[/B] install the ZIP from TWRP. Do not write the loose system.img directly to MTD14. The installer empties the existing system UBIFS volume, copies the ROM, and writes the MTK-formatted boot image. It does not replace TWRP.

[COLOR="Red"][SIZE="5"][CENTER]Do not mirror the download without permission.[/CENTER][/SIZE][/COLOR]

