[SIZE="4"][B]Changelog[/B][/SIZE]

[B]2026-10-24 — Beta 1[/B]

[LIST]
[*]Voice calls work: the modem no longer crashes at call start (two speech settings from the Y330 audio HAL are adapted for the Y220 modem)
[*]Video recording (640x480 MPEG-4 with AMR-WB audio)
[*]Wi-Fi hotspot (kernel #98) and USB tethering (IPv6 enabled in the kernel)
[*]Original Huawei charging animation with the phone off
[*]Bluetooth pairing, A2DP and headset calls tested; factory Bluetooth address
[*]Camera: no more hang when leaving the app right after taking a picture
[*]Network after boot: fixed a race in the MediaTek RIL that left the radio off in about half of the boots (10 of 10 boots registered in testing)
[*]USB: after a clean install the phone shows up as mass storage with adb (before, it could be left with USB off)
[*]Tested from a clean install following the steps in this post
[*]Modem recovery: if the modem crashes, it is restarted automatically and the phone is back on the network in about 40 seconds, no reboot needed
[/LIST]

[B]2026-10-23 — Alpha 1 (not released)[/B]

[LIST]
[*]First CyanogenMod 10.1 build, tested on real Y220-U05 hardware
[*]Android 4.2.2 MediaTek userspace from the Y330-U01: Mali GPU, RIL, audio, camera, Bluetooth
[*]Wi-Fi WPA fix in the wlan_mt6582 kernel module
[*]Microphone, camera capture, signal strength, APNs, zram and touch keys fixed during bring-up
[/LIST]

